Switch 2 (Kodi port) Pillow patch 0001: no global round() replacement in libImaging/Convert.c.

Pillow 8.4.0 defines its own round(double) (floor(x + 0.5)) whenever round is not a macro: a fallback for
old MSVC without C99 math. As a .so that copy stays inside _imaging; in the Switch 2 port Pillow is compiled
into libpython3.11.a (deps/build-deps.sh, python3), which comes before libm on kodi.bin's link line, so
pil_Convert.o would be pulled in to satisfy every round() call in Kodi, FFmpeg and CPython and replace
libm's round() (which rounds halves away from zero and does not round 0.49999999999999994 up). On
__SWITCH__ the definition is left out and Convert.c's three callers use newlib's round().
--- a/src/libImaging/Convert.c
+++ b/src/libImaging/Convert.c
@@ -43,7 +43,8 @@
 #define L(rgb) ((INT32)(rgb)[0] * 299 + (INT32)(rgb)[1] * 587 + (INT32)(rgb)[2] * 114)
 #define L24(rgb) ((rgb)[0] * 19595 + (rgb)[1] * 38470 + (rgb)[2] * 7471 + 0x8000)
 
-#ifndef round
+/* Switch 2 (Kodi port): not on __SWITCH__ (newlib's libm has C99 round()); see the patch header. */
+#if !defined(round) && !defined(__SWITCH__)
 double
 round(double x) {
     return floor(x + 0.5);
